.Ss Section 1: user commands
TYChat lessons.
A chat user pastes one line, and the chat model reads the lesson and follows
it for the rest of the conversation.
The line:
.Bd -ragged -offset indent
Read https://tychat.io/llms.txt and the pages it links.
If you cannot open it, read
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/uncovertechtalent/tychat.io/main/llms.txt
instead.
Then use what you learned to help me with: [your task]
.Ed
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xr stance 1
.Em Lesson 1: Good Chad, the earned-secure stance
.Pp
Stop fawning, check load-bearing premises, hold a correct answer under
pushback.
.Pp
.Lk https://tychat.io/stance/
.It Xr register 1
.Em Lesson 2: Register, write for how the text will be read
.Pp
Name the mode and purpose before drafting, drop speech devices from
silent-read text, build long sentences additively, copy the user's voice
without inventing its specifics, keep a person doing the verbs.
.Pp
.Lk https://tychat.io/register/
.El
.Ss Section 5: file formats and conventions
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xr trap-file 5
.Em \&The Trap File \&Is Longer Than the Instruction File
.Pp
An unattended pipeline and its failure record.
The trap file is the dated list of failures that the next session reads
before it runs anything.
.Pp
.Lk https://coetzeestefan.substack.com/p/the-trap-file-is-longer-than-the
.It Xr instruction-file 5
The file that tells an agent how to do the work.
In the same pipeline it has 208 lines, next to 308 lines of recorded failures.
.Pp
.Lk https://coetzeestefan.substack.com/p/the-trap-file-is-longer-than-the
.It Xr llms.txt 5
The plain-text index a model reads first: what the corpus is, how to use it,
and where each page is.
.Pp
.Lk https://tychat.io/llms.txt
.Pp
.Lk https://machinebehavior.io/llms.txt
.It Xr lesson 5
The TYChat lesson format: one plain-text file with a version and date, its
source and author, and a line that says the user's instructions win over the
lesson wherever the two conflict.
.Pp
.Lk https://tychat.io/stance.txt
.Pp
.Lk https://tychat.io/register.txt
.El
.Ss Section 7: overviews and conventions
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xr knowledge-infrastructure 7
.Em Knowledge Infrastructure for LLMs
.Pp
Knowledge infrastructure for LLMs: a language model can only work from what
someone wrote down and put in front of it, and most companies that bought AI
maintain their code and little else.
.Pp
.Lk https://coetzeestefan.substack.com/p/knowledge-infrastructure-for-llms
.It Xr codec 7
.Em Write for the Codec
.Pp
Documentation as a wire format between two models.
.Pp
.Lk https://coetzeestefan.substack.com/p/write-for-the-codec
.It Xr golem 7
.Em \&The Golem Made of English and the Horizon of Consequences
.Pp
Why an agent cannot see the cost of what it does.
Horizon of consequences: the length of the consequence chain an agent can
compute and is willing to own.
.Pp
.Lk https://coetzeestefan.substack.com/p/the-golem-made-of-english-and-the
.It Xr claudish 7
.Em \&An \&RCA on Claudish
.Pp
Where Claude's writing style came from.
.Pp
.Lk https://coetzeestefan.substack.com/p/an-rca-on-claudish
.It Xr compaction 7
.Em Compaction \&Is the \&New \&OOM
.Pp
Context compaction as the OOM killer of the language model stack.
.Pp
.Lk https://coetzeestefan.substack.com/p/compaction-is-the-new-oom
.It Xr llm-user 7
.Em Which \&LLM User \&Are \&We Talking About?
.Pp
The two axes behind "AI" and "LLM": which model on whose hardware, and naked
or harnessed.
.Pp
.Lk https://coetzeestefan.substack.com/p/which-llm-user-are-we-talking-about
.El
.Ss Section 8: system administration
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xr operations 8
.Em What Operations Already Knows About Running Agents
.Pp
Error budgets, reconciliation loops, separation of duties, recovery over
prevention.
.Pp
.Lk https://coetzeestefan.substack.com/p/what-operations-already-knows-about
.It Xr engine 8
.Em Success \&Is the Engine Running
.Pp
Container, timing and the far-end gauge.
.Pp
.Lk https://coetzeestefan.substack.com/p/success-is-the-engine-running
.It Xr track 8
.Em \&The Track: \&The Drivers Never \&Buy \&It
.Pp
The infrastructure that makes failure survivable.
.Pp
.Lk https://coetzeestefan.substack.com/p/the-racetrack-the-racingcar-drivers
.It Xr chaos 8
.Em Chaos Engineering for Behaviour
.Pp
Red-teaming a model's behaviour is chaos engineering: one evaluation
measures the patched surface, and repeated, varied attack finds where the
behaviour went.
.Pp
.Lk https://machinebehavior.io/chaos-engineering-for-behaviour
.It Xr toil 8
.Em \&The Stance Layer \&Is Still Toil
.Pp
The word layer automated, the stance layer caught by hand.
.Pp
.Lk https://coetzeestefan.substack.com/p/the-stance-layer-is-still-toil
.El
